From 7b534bfaa185a88afb59c47b3fdb83824a747d4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:50:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add phishing_pot historical corpus as a domain-reputation
 source

Adds known_phishing_indicators table (schema.sql, auto-applied on
next connect like the jarm_json column was) plus a one-time offline
loader (backend/scripts/load_phishing_pot.py) that extracts just the
sender/URL domains out of the 8,614 rf-peixoto/phishing_pot .eml
samples -- the raw 623MB dataset never touches git or gets a live
pipeline run against it.

domain_reputation.check_phishing_pot_corpus() reads the resulting
table and check_domain_reputation() treats a hit exactly like a
Spamhaus DBL hit (high risk, added to found_on_lists/evidence). This
is a static historical blocklist signal, intentionally kept separate
from threat_correlation_engine.py's live cross-user campaign
correlation -- the two answer different questions and shouldn't be
conflated.
